Hyper Math (`libhypermath`)
===========================

Hyper Math is a clean-room C++20 numerical, scientific, and relational columnar
computing library engineered in compliance with the **GNU Coding Standards** and
licensed under the **GNU General Public License v3.0 or later (GPLv3+)**.

It unifies the capabilities of four foundational Python data-science libraries
within a single, zero-dependency C++20 architecture:

1. **NumPy Equivalent (`hyper_math::tensor`)**
   - **Rank-Agnostic Affine Lattice Engine**: Arbitrary N-dimensional shapes and
     byte/element strides over 64-byte cache-line aligned reference-counted slab
     buffers (`slab_buffer<T>`).
   - **Zero-Copy Views & Contradiction-Free Broadcasting**: Slicing, transposition,
     reshaping, axis squeezing/expansion, and multi-operand stride broadcasting.
   - **Lazily Fused Morphism Expressions (`ufunc`)**: Compile-time expression
     templates that fuse elementwise arithmetic and transcendental operations
     (`sin`, `cos`, `exp`, `log`, `sqrt`, `pow`, `clip`, `where`) into a single
     allocation-free pass.
   - **Reductions, Manipulation & Contractions**: Full, axis-specific, and
     NaN-safe reductions (`sum`/`nansum`, `mean`/`nanmean`, `var`/`nanvar`,
     `std_dev`/`nanstd`, `min`/`nanmin`, `max`/`nanmax`, `argmin`/`nanargmin`,
     `argmax`/`nanargmax`, `cumsum`/`nancumsum`, `cumprod`/`nancumprod`,
     `median`/`nanmedian`, `percentile`/`nanpercentile`, `quantile`/`nanquantile`),
     array manipulation (`meshgrid`, `tile`, `repeat`, `pad`, `flip`, `roll`,
     `rot90`, `tril`, `triu`, `vander`, `searchsorted`, `bincount`, `histogram`,
     `histogram2d`, `histogramdd`, `gradient`, `cov`, `corrcoef`, `polyfit`,
     `polyval`, `polydiv`, `sliding_window_view`), matrix contractions (`matmul`,
     `dot`, `vdot`, `inner`, `outer`, `kron`, `tensordot`, `multi_dot`),
     generalized Einstein summation (`einsum`, `einsum_path`), and `.npy` /
     `.npz` binary serialization (`save_npy`, `load_npy`, `save_npz`, `load_npz`).

2. **SciPy Equivalent (`hyper_math::scientific`)**
   - **`linalg`**: LU (`lu`), symmetric indefinite `ldl`, Householder &
     column-pivoted QR (`qr`, `qr_pivoted`, `rq`, `qz`), Cholesky, Hessenberg,
     Schur (`schur`, `rsf2csf`), symmetric & general eigensolvers (`eigh`,
     `eigh_generalized`, `eigh_tridiagonal`, `eig`, `eigvals`), SVD (`svd`,
     `svdvals`, `diagsvd`, `subspace_angles`), Moore-Penrose pseudoinverse
     (`pinv`), determinant (`det`, `slogdet`), inverse (`inv`), least squares
     (`lstsq`), matrix functions (`expm`, `expm_frechet`,
     `fractional_matrix_power`, `funm`, `cosm`, `sinm`, `tanm`, `coshm`,
     `sinhm`, `tanhm`, `signm`, `sqrtm`, `logm_spd`, `polar`), banded solvers
     (`solve_banded`, `cholesky_banded`), Sylvester/Lyapunov/Riccati solvers,
     and structured matrices (`toeplitz`, `circulant`, `hankel`, `hilbert`,
     `invhilbert`, `hadamard`, `companion`, `leslie`, `fiedler`, `pascal`,
     `helmert`, `dft_matrix`, `khatri_rao`, `clarkson_woodruff_transform`).
   - **`fft`**: Mixed-radix Cooley-Tukey and Bluestein Chirp-Z arbitrary-length
     1D, 2D, and N-D Fast Fourier Transforms (`fft`, `ifft`, `rfft`, `irfft`,
     `hfft`, `ihfft`, `fft2`, `ifft2`, `rfft2`, `irfft2`, `fftn`, `ifftn`,
     `rfftn`, `irfftn`), Type-I..IV Discrete Cosine & Sine Transforms (`dct`,
     `idct`, `dct2`, `idct2`, `dst`, `idst`), Fast Hankel Transform (`fht`,
     `ifht`), and fast FFT convolution (`convolve_fft`).
   - **`integrate`**: Adaptive Gauss-Kronrod G7-K15 1D/2D/3D/N-D quadrature
     (`quad`, `quad_vec`, `dblquad`, `tplquad`, `nquad`), `tanhsinh`, Romberg,
     Gauss-Legendre, composite Simpson's/trapezoidal rules, adaptive RK4(5),
     RK23, DOP853, & stiff implicit Radau/BDF ODE solvers with event detection
     (`solve_ivp`, `solve_ivp_events`), and two-point BVP solver (`solve_bvp`).
   - **`optimize`**: Root finding (`brentq`, `brenth`, `ridder`, `secant`,
     `halley`, `fixed_point`, `fsolve`, `broyden1`), scalar & multivariable
     optimization (BFGS, L-BFGS-B, CG, Newton-CG, Powell, Dogleg, Trust-NCG,
     Nelder-Mead, SLSQP), nonlinear & bounded least squares (`least_squares_lm`,
     `least_squares_bounds`, `curve_fit`, `nnls`, `lsq_linear`), Simplex LP &
     branch-and-bound MILP (`linprog`, `milp`), global optimizers
     (`dual_annealing`, `differential_evolution`, `basinhopping`, `shgo`,
     `direct`), and linear/quadratic assignment (`linear_sum_assignment`,
     `quadratic_assignment`).
   - **`stats`**: Complete special function suite (Gamma, Polygamma, Beta, Error
     functions, Dawson, Fresnel, Sine/Cosine/Exponential integrals, Spence,
     Lambert W, Wright Omega, Hurwitz/Riemann Zeta, Airy, Bessel `jv`/`yv`/`kv`/
     `iv`, spherical Bessel, associated Legendre, spherical harmonics,
     orthogonal polynomials, hypergeometric `hyp2f1`/`hyp1f1`, complete
     elliptic integrals), 22 univariate/discrete/multivariate distributions
     (`multivariate_normal_dist`, `dirichlet_dist`, `wishart_dist`),
     Quasi-Monte Carlo (`qmc::halton`, `qmc::sobol`, `qmc::latin_hypercube`,
     `qmc::poisson_disk`, `qmc::discrepancy`), bootstrap/permutation/Monte-Carlo
     hypothesis testing, 25+ statistical tests, Gaussian KDE, and PCA.
   - **`spatial` & `cluster`**: Clean-room $k$-d Tree (`kd_tree`), 15-metric
     `cdist`/`pdist`/`squareform`, 2D Convex Hull, Delaunay triangulation
     (`delaunay_2d`), Voronoi & Spherical Voronoi diagrams, Halfspace
     Intersection, Boolean polygon clipping, 3D `rotation` (quaternions, Euler
     angles, SLERP, Kabsch alignment) & `rigid_transform`, $k$-Means++
     (`kmeans2`), hierarchical clustering (`linkage`, `fcluster`, `cophenet`,
     `optimal_leaf_ordering`), `dbscan`, and `optics`.
   - **`interpolate`, `signal`, `sparse`**: Cubic/Akima/PCHIP/Hermite/B-splines
     (`bspline`, `make_interp_spline`, `make_lsq_spline`, `make_smoothing_spline`,
     `splprep`, `splev`), RBF & 2D/3D grid interpolation, FIR & IIR filters
     (Butterworth, Chebyshev I/II, Elliptic, Bessel, notch/peak, SOS), Welch/
     Lomb-Scargle/STFT/CZT spectral analysis, LTI state-space systems
     (`lti_system`, `lsim`, `step_response`, `impulse_response`, `bode`), and
     CSR/CSC/COO/DIA/BSR/DOK/LIL sparse matrices with CG, BiCGSTAB, GMRES,
     MINRES, LSQR, LU/ILU, `eigsh`/`svds`, and `csgraph` graph algorithms.
   - **`autograd` (Forward & Reverse-Mode Automatic Differentiation)**:
     Dual numbers (`dual_number`), Wengert reverse-mode computation tape (`tape`
     & `var`), exact scalar derivatives (`derivative`), directional gradients
     (`forward_grad`), Jacobians (`jacobian`), reverse-mode gradients (`grad`,
     `value_and_grad`), second-order Hessians (`hessian`), and analytical-gradient
     BFGS optimization (`minimize_bfgs_autograd`).

3. **Pandas & Polars Equivalent (`hyper_math::tabular`)**
   - **Dual-Bitmask Columnar Memory**: Every `series` pairs a contiguous typed
     tensor buffer (`int64_t`, `double`, `bool`, or UTF-8 strings) with a
     64-bit word-aligned `validity_bitmap` accelerated via hardware
     `std::popcount` and bitwise intrinsics.
   - **Pandas Index Alignment & Windowing**: Bi-directional hash-indexed axis
     labels (`index_axis`) supporting `loc` (label-based) and `iloc`
     (positional) indexing, automatic label alignment in arithmetic, missing-data
     imputation (`drop_nulls`, `fill_null`, `fill_forward`, `fill_backward`,
     linear `interpolate`), rolling and EWM windows (`rolling_mean`,
     `rolling_sum`, `rolling_min`, `rolling_max`, `rolling_std`, `ewm_mean`),
     `value_counts`, `is_in`, `drop_duplicates`, `sample`, `corr`, `pivot`,
     `melt`, `concat_rows`, RFC-4180 CSV I/O, and Hyper Math Binary (`.hmb`)
     columnar serialization (`write_hmb`, `read_hmb`).
   - **Polars Declarative Lazy Query Engine (`lazy_frame` & `expr`)**:
     Expression AST (`col("x") * lit(2.0)`, `when().then().otherwise()`,
     partitioned window functions `.over("group")`, aggregations) backed by a
     rule-based algebraic query optimizer implementing **Predicate Pushdown**,
     **Projection Pushdown (Column Pruning)**, **Filter Fusion**, and
     **Constant Folding**, executing over vectorized hash joins and hash
     group-by aggregations.

Building and Testing
--------------------

```sh
./configure     # Generate pkg-config hyper-math.pc
make            # Build libhypermath.a, libhypermath.so, CLI, tests, and benchmarks
make check      # Run the complete unit & CLI verification suite
make bench      # Run the multi-threaded performance benchmark suite
./bin/hyper-math --version
./bin/hyper-math --demo
./bin/hyper-math --repl
```

